# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).
## [version] - year-month-day
### Added
- Makefile BLAS/LAPACK auto-detection across Accelerate, OpenBLAS, MKL, conda, Homebrew, system and reference libraries, with `BLAS_BACKEND`, `BLAS_LIBS` and `BLAS=0` overrides
- Opt-in `make deps-blas` / `make BLAS_BACKEND=download` target that downloads, checksum-verifies and builds OpenBLAS locally under `external/`
- CMake BLAS/LAPACK detection with `HEATFLOW_BLAS`, `HEATFLOW_BLAS_BACKEND`, `HEATFLOW_BLAS_LIBRARIES` and opt-in `HEATFLOW_BLAS_DOWNLOAD` options
- fpm wrapper scripts `build_fpm.sh` and `build_fpm_with_petsc.sh`, sharing the Makefile BLAS/LAPACK detection and opt-in OpenBLAS download
### Changed
- Makefile now auto-detects MPI Fortran wrappers from `PATH` and common install prefixes instead of only `/usr/bin`
- CMake now smoke-tests compiler candidates and skips broken wrappers such as incomplete conda MPI installations
### Deprecated
### Removed
### Fixed
- Makefile builds no longer fail with `cannot find -lblas` when no system BLAS/LAPACK is installed; BLAS/LAPACK are optional for the current sources
- fpm.toml is compatible with fpm 0.10+ again by removing the unsupported `[features]`/`[profiles]` sections; optional external modules are declared explicitly
- PETSc 3.23+ Fortran null-object handling now uses `PetscObjectIsNull()` and avoids assigning `PETSC_NULL_*` to `Mat`/`Vec`/`KSP` objects, fixing `Cannot create PETSC_NULL_XXX object` with PETSc 3.26
### Security

##[2.1.0] - 2026-10-28
## Added
- Runtime solver selection via the `solver` input flag: `legacy` (original conjugate gradient solver) or the PETSc preconditioners `ilu`, `lu` and `gamg`. Default: `ilu`
- `T_decimals` input parameter controlling the number of decimal places written to the temperature output file (e.g. `3` writes `100.001` and `1000.001`). Default: `3`
- Support for compiling without PETSc when the libraries are not available (legacy-solver-only build); auto-detected by the Makefile and CMake, or forced with `make PETSC=0` / `-DHEATFLOW_PETSC=OFF`
- Early validation at startup that the selected solver is available in the current build
- `-i` and `-o` command line options to select the input and output directories (default `./inputs` and `./outputs`); the output directory is created if it does not exist
- macOS build support: Makefile Darwin block (Homebrew PETSc, Apple Accelerate BLAS), CMake compiler auto-detection and `COMPILER_ID`-based flags, `PETSC_DIR`/`PETSC_ARCH` fallback
- Directory selection command line options: `-i`/`--input-directory`, `-o`/`--output-directory` and the `--directory` alias (maps to `<dir>/inputs`, `<dir>/outputs`, `<dir>/restart`); the restart directory is configurable via `restart_dir`
- HDF5 output support: `_HDF5Output` input flag writes `times` and `temperatures` datasets (GZIP compressed) to `output_<RunName>.h5`; enabled at build time with `make USE_HDF5=1` or `-DHEATFLOW_HDF5=ON`
- `build_fpm_with_petsc.sh` helper for fpm builds with PETSc

## Changed
- The PETSc preconditioner is now selected at runtime via `solver` instead of the compile-time `PRECONDITIONER` parameter (previously fixed to GAMG)
- CMake build now includes the PETSc solver module and links MPI
- PETSc objects are now nullified at runtime instead of declaration-time (required for newer PETSc, e.g. macOS Homebrew)
- fpm.toml no longer hardcodes PETSc paths; include/library paths are provided at build time

## Fixed
- LU direct solver no longer fails with "preonly doesn't make sense with nonzero initial guess" (nonzero initial guess is now only used for the iterative solvers)

